        "uuid": "7f96bb07_b03b8bcf",
        "filename": "keystone/application_credential/controllers.py",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 8482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T11:09:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes - will add a comment. Also open to suggestions on what the right length should really be. I guess I could make it 66 bytes and then not chop the padding.",
      "parentUuid": "7f96bb07_fca905df",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "470538c1c5e79038bd07ec33b2a39b4a6e22eebf",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f96bb07_761178ac",
        "filename": "keystone/application_credential/controllers.py",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T15:00:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something like this might be safer: \n\nhttps://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/token/providers/fernet/token_formatters.py#L78-L79\n\nBecause tokens are variable length, the padding can also fluctuate. Since we\u0027re dealing with a fixed length we probably don\u0027t have to worry about it as much, but from the comment it doesn\u0027t look like padding is url-safe (I\u0027d need to dig up real references).",
      "parentUuid": "7f96bb07_b03b8bcf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "470538c1c5e79038bd07ec33b2a39b4a6e22eebf",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f96bb07_563b1cea",
        "filename": "keystone/application_credential/controllers.py",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 8482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T15:10:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I took this from http://git.openstack.org/cgit/openstack/keystone/tree/keystone/token/providers/common.py#n62 but rstrip works just as well, will change it.\n\nI think the padding isn\u0027t url-safe because \u003d is used for query parameters, e.g. GET /v3/users?name\u003dcmurphy\n\nWe\u0027re not actually using this in a url ourselves and probably no one should send an application secret as part of a url. I\u0027m not really totally sure we need to strip the padding for tokens since as of v3 they\u0027re only sent as headers, not part of a url. But in any case it looks kind of weird to me to keep the padding and we don\u0027t need it for anything since we\u0027re not going to decode it.",
      "parentUuid": "7f96bb07_761178ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "470538c1c5e79038bd07ec33b2a39b4a6e22eebf",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f96bb07_79b96be7",
        "filename": "keystone/application_credential/controllers.py",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T15:25:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All good points - but +1 for consistency.",
      "parentUuid": "7f96bb07_563b1cea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "470538c1c5e79038bd07ec33b2a39b4a6e22eebf",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
